  "name": "Wind Release: Rakshasa Barrier",
  "type": "jutsu",
  "img": "icons/svg/book.svg",
  "system": {
    "identifier": "wind-release-rakshasa-barrier",
    "description": "<p>You raise your hand and generate an intensely dense torrent of wind that circles around you, creating a bubble of wind that envelops your entire body.</p>\n<p>The barrier that envelops you has 2d12 + 6 hit points, resistance to Lightning damage and vulnerability to Fire damage.</p>\n<p>If this jutsu would reduce damage from any of the listed damage types below, it will trigger an additional effect. Creatures in 15-foot radius centered on you must make a Dexterity saving throw to resist its effects.</p>\n<p>Fire. All creatures make a saving throw becoming Burned on a failed save as the Fire spreads around you from your rotating bubble of wind.</p>\n<p>Lightning. All creatures must make a saving throw becoming Shocked on a failed save, as lightning jumps from you to other creatures around you.</p>\n<p>Cold. All creatures must make a saving throw becoming Chilled on a failed save, as the cold is spread to all creatures around you.</p>\n<p>Earth. All creatures must make a saving throw, gaining the Bleed condition on a failed save, as they are pelted with shrapnel of earth.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above C-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3 and the barriers hit points by +6.</p>",
